RegistrationService.java: Effective Hold Status
static String effectiveStatus(Registration r) {
return r.status.equals("PENDING_PAYMENT")
&& !r.expiresAt.isAfter(Instant.now())
? "EXPIRED"
: r.status;
}
Expiry is interpreted when records are read and when payment is attempted. A pending record whose
deadline has passed no longer occupies a seat. This avoids relying on a background timer to make
capacity available. Payment confirmation locks the same event and rechecks the registration before
changing its state.
The SQL schema adds a second consistency barrier through a unique student-event pair. Transactions
provide ordered updates; the constraint prevents duplicate records even if an incorrect caller attempts a
repeated insert. Cancellation preserves history rather than deleting the booking.
